.TH DANBY-WEIGHTCHANGE 1
.SH NAME
danby-weightchange \- body-mass energy-balance model
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B danby/weightchange
.SH MODEL
M'=(E-a M^(3/4)-cM)/q.
.PP
M is body mass, E energy intake, aM^(3/4) a metabolic scaling law, cM an
activity expenditure, and q effective stored-energy density.  An equilibrium
occurs where intake and expenditure intersect.  The equation illustrates
feedback and timescale; it is not individualized health advice.
.SH DISPLAY
The graph uses physical stock magnitude rather than a normalized population
fraction.  The current mass bar is directly editable.
.SH CONTROLS
Tracks set intake, basal coefficient, activity, and energy density.  Space
pauses, period steps, r resets, and q exits.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/plugin/weightchange.b
.br
.B /appl/danby/weightchange.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR populationmodel (2),
.IR numerics (2)
